BOM Excel Download Template 
 
 The Bom.vm velocity template is an example for downloading a single BOM into 
excel.  

The template has the follwing variables defined in its context 

	1. $ISO8601 - The ISO8601 class useful to format dates as text by 
				  calling the safeFormat function 
	2. $STRESC - Utility class to csv escape text data (org.apache.commons.lang.StringEscapeUtils)
	3. $date - The DateTool class http://velocity.apache.org/tools/devel/javadoc/org/apache/velocity/tools/generic/DateTool.html
	4. $CONFIG - The ConfigurationUtils class to access configuration information
	5. $responsibilities - The responsibilities to be displayed. (An array 
					from the property pcm.bom.excel.display.responsibilities) 
	6. $defectTypes - The list of defect types defined in the system
	7. $isAttritionRateEnabled - If attrition rates are allowed in the system
	8. $isLeadTimeEnabled - If lead time is enabled. (Value of property pcm.bom.include.leadTime)
	9. $helper - A helper class to display BOM Data in this template easier
   10. $bomDetails - A map with details of the BOM being downloaded (selected BOM)
   11. $dp - An iterable over BOM Lines under the selected BOM
	 
 In order to successfully download and upload the BOM, the excel workbook must 
have a template sheet called "Bom" (no quotes). This sheet will require two 
header rows. The first rown should contain keys (with no spaces between words) 
for each column and the second header row can contain human readable headers. 
The actual data is populated from row three. The keys in the first row are used 
as keys into the data for BOM lines. This allows us to easily create the XML 
markup required to upload the BOM into the system. Certain data is required by 
the Item import mechanism as defined by the ItemMessage.xsd 


$bomDetails
===========
The $bomDetails variable is a Map that contains details of the selected BOM.
 * $bomDetails.get("selectedBom") - The selected BOM
 * $bomDetails.get("responsibilitiesMap") - A Map<String,List<ItemAssignment>> for 
	responsibilities assigned to the Item pointed to by the selected BOM 

$helper
=======
The $helper variable is an instance of a helper class to easily display BOM line 
data. All data is escaped and rendered comma delimited 

Methods on $helper
------------------
* getAttritionRatesHeaderKeys() - Displays the defect types prepended with AR_. 
	This can be used as keys for the first row in excel. The ordering in defined 
	by the ordering in the $defectTypes variable 
* getAttritionRatesDisplayHeaders() - Displays the defect types. Can be used as 
	human readable headers for defect types in the second row in excel. The ordering 
	in defined by the ordering in the $defectTypes variable 
* getResponsibilityHeaderKeys() - Display the displayResponsibilities prefixed 
	with RESP_. This can be used as keys for the first row in excel. 
* getResponsibilityDisplayHeaders() - Display the display responsibilities. Can be 
	used as human readable headers for defect types in the second row in excel. 
* printAttritionRateData(final Map<PcmDefectType, PcmBomLineAttritionRate> arData) - Prints 
	the attrition rates across all defect types. The ordering in defined by the ordering 
	in the $defectTypes variable 
* printResponsibilityData(Map<String, List<ItemAssignment>> responsibilitiesMap) - Prints 
	responsibilities (userIds) given a map of responsibility assignments 
	for an item. If multiple users are assigned the same responsibility, the user 
	ids appear in the same column under the responsibility key. 
* printItemPlatforms(Item item) - Print the platform names an item belongs to in one column
* printItemCategories(Item item) - Print the item category ids an item belongs to

$dp
===
 This is the data provider injected into the velocity template. The data 
provider is an iterable over a Map<String,Object>. This can be iterated over 
using the #foreach tag in velocity. The structure of the Map for each element is 
as follows 

Key -> Value
------------
level -> The level of the BOM line. The selected BOM must always be displayed as 
	Level 1. This level marks the hierarchical position in the BOM Tree for the 
	current BOM Line 
bomLine -> The BomLine object representing the current BOM line
attritionRatesMap -> A Map<PcmDefectType, PcmBomLineAttritionRate> representing 
	attrition rate data for the item of the BOM Line. Use the helper method 
	printAttritionRateData(final Map<PcmDefectType, PcmBomLineAttritionRate> arData) 
	to display attrition rate information. 
responsibilitiesMap -> A Map<String, List<ItemAssignment>> of assignments by 
	responsibility for the item of the BOM Line. Use the helper method 
	printResponsibilityData(Map<String, List<ItemAssignment>> responsibilitiesMap) 
	to display responsibility assignments. 

